     bbuuss__ggeenneerriicc__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd() prints out the default device announcement mes‐
     sage.  Given device ‘foo0’ on bus ‘bar0’ where foo0 has the description
     “FooCard 1234” and is associated with the NUMA domain 1, the following
     would be printed:

           foo0: <FooCard 1234> numa-domain 1 on bar0

     bbuuss__ggeenneerriicc__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd() calls the three helper functions
     bbuuss__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd__hheeaaddeerr(), bbuuss__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd__ddoommaaiinn(), and
     bbuuss__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd__ffooootteerr().

     bbuuss__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd__hheeaaddeerr() outputs the device name and unit followed by the
     device description in angle brackets (“foo0: <FooCard 1234>”).

     bbuuss__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd__ddoommaaiinn() outputs “ numa-domain” followed by the domain
     number if bbuuss__ggeett__ddoommaaiinn() returns a valid domain for the device
     (“numa-domain 1”).  If _d_e_v is not associated witha valid domain, nothing
     is output.

     bbuuss__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd__ffooootteerr() outputs the string “ on” followed by the parent
     device's name and unit (“ on bar0”).

     These functions can be used to implement BUS_PRINT_CHILD(9) in a bus
     driver if bbuuss__ggeenneerriicc__pprriinntt__cchhiilldd() is not sufficient.

